From f382248f0d025038babfa52f44158bca3c5e86cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:43:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-qc49-hpvq-g2w6 (CVE-2026-129289): drain unread
 request bodies

Opening php://input could create a request body stream without consuming
the input from the SAPI; request shutdown treated the stream as proof
that the body was read and skipped the drain, so unread FastCGI STDIN
bytes could be parsed as another request on a FCGI_KEEP_CONN connection.
Drain whenever post_read is false, and reject a new FastCGI request if
the previous STDIN record was only partially consumed.

Backport of php-src c7a30157f6 for EOL 7.4.33. Differences for 7.4:
- the SAPI.c hunk lands in sapi_deactivate() (8.2: sapi_deactivate_module);
  code is otherwise identical, hunks apply with small offsets
- the two FPM tests use strpos() instead of str_contains() (PHP 8.0+)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
