From ac795bc65c617082a48f5d6ef6883f68ec10c6dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:52:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-f6gg-rchx-xw8j (CVE-2026-128064): mixed-case HTTPS
 and FTPS downgrade to plaintext

The http and ftp wrappers decided whether to use TLS by looking at a
single lower-case 's' at a fixed offset of the scheme, so "HTTPS://" or
"FTPS://" URLs (the wrapper lookup is case-insensitive) were sent in
plaintext, including credentials and request bodies. Compare the whole
scheme case-insensitively.

Backport of php-src 9c0b44ffd6 for EOL 7.4.33. Differences for 7.4:
- uses zend_string_equals_literal_ci() on the zend_string scheme as
  upstream, but keeps the resource->scheme NULL guard in the http wrapper
  too (upstream dropped it there)
- tests rewritten for 7.4's ServerClientTestCase.inc, which has no
  phpt_notify_server_start(), {{ ADDR }} or notify messages: fixed ports
  64331/64332, the server worker writes what it saw to a temp file that
  the client process prints; the HTTPS server only checks the first byte
  for a TLS ClientHello (0x16)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
