Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-5j3f-64r7-f564 (CVE-2026-129538): PATH_INFO
 underflow in CGI init_request_info()

When the suffix stripped from SCRIPT_FILENAME (or PATH_TRANSLATED) was
longer than PATH_INFO, the re-derived PATH_INFO pointed before the value
and was then read, written and copied from. Only rewrite PATH_INFO when
it is longer than the stripped suffix, as FPM has done since the
CVE-2019-11043 fix (fpm_main.c already has that check and is untouched).

Backport of php-src 1e109bfbd2 for EOL 7.4.33. The code change is
identical (applies with offset). The test is taken unchanged; it uses
proc_open() with an array command, which exists since PHP 7.4.0.

