From 5539c2a7b60e8c5ed60006e2dfa7290b9606a16e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:28:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-85c2-q967-79q5 (CVE-2026-6722): stale SOAP ref_map
 pointer with Apache Map

SOAP_GLOBAL(ref_map) stored decoded values for href lookups without
holding a reference. When decoding an Apache Map freed such a value, a
later lookup used the freed zval: a use-after-free reachable from a SOAP
message (SoapServer request or SoapClient response). The map now holds a
reference and releases it when it is reset.

Backport of php-src aee3b3ac9b (Ilija Tovilo), same change as Sury's 7.4
patch 0128.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
