From 0dff4bf501dd885efad05405c641b94b4b012730 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:28:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-rgrp-mwpx-f6rm: unbounded recursion in SOAP XML
 parsing and decoding

A deeply nested SOAP document, or a long or cyclic chain of href
references, recursed without limit in cleanup_xml_node() and in the
decoder and crashed the worker on stack exhaustion. cleanup_xml_node() is
now iterative, documents nested deeper than SOAP_MAX_XML_DEPTH (2048) are
rejected with libxml2 before 2.13 (newer libxml2 limits depth itself),
and decoding, which follows href references, stops with a SOAP error past
SOAP_MAX_DECODE_DEPTH.

Backport of php-src 3655b79c7b (Alexandre Daubois), Sury's 7.4 patch
0153. One hunk is merged by hand: the iterative cleanup_xml_node() keeps
the XML_DTD_NODE branch that the GHSA-4646-p932-gw34 fix in this branch
added, as in Sury's later patch 0205.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
