+GET /index.php): failed to open stream: HTTP wrapper full URI path does not allow CR or LF characters in %s on line %d
From 4f13331d6e35f81742961bbfb86125b02bf67ffd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:26:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-v8xr-gpvj-cx9g (CVE-2025-1217): http response header
 folding

The http wrapper treated a folded (continuation) response header line
as a new header, so a server could smuggle a Location or Content-Type
past the parser. Folded lines are now joined onto the header they
continue, as RFC 7230 describes. http_response_header_05.phpt tested
the old behaviour and is removed upstream.

Backport of php-src d20b4c97a9 (Jakub Zelenka), Sury's 7.4 patch 0106.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ext/openssl/tests/ServerClientTestCase.inc    |  65 +++-
 ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c             | 347 ++++++++++++------
 .../tests/http/ghsa-v8xr-gpvj-cx9g-001.phpt   |  49 +++
 .../tests/http/ghsa-v8xr-gpvj-cx9g-002.phpt   |  51 +++
