From 2575f468de6b1365bfc29635f5e633b7f0b075de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:26:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-52jp-hrpf-2jff (CVE-2025-1861): redirect Location
 truncation

The Location header was copied into a 1024-byte buffer and cut there,
so a long redirect target was followed truncated, to a URL the server
never sent. It is now kept on the heap, and a Location longer than 8182
bytes (8192 minus "Location: ") fails the request.

Backport of php-src ac1a054bb3 (Jakub Zelenka), Sury's 7.4 patch 0108.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
