From 01aa10528d5e148bfec863df17b5c822f205405b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:26:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-hgf5-96fm-v528 (CVE-2025-1736): user header check
 needs CRLF

To decide whether the user already set Host, User-Agent, Content-Type
and so on, the http wrapper looked for the name at the start of the
header bag or after any LF. A bare LF inside another header's value
("X-Foo: a\nhost: b") therefore counted as a set header, and PHP left
out its own. The name now has to follow CRLF.

Backport of php-src 41d49abbd9 (Jakub Zelenka), Sury's 7.4 patch 0109.

