From d74cb3d0f2e1067456f9fbc7cd9c0125cd064f28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:26:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-fpwc-w8rq-cr92 (CVE-2026-91766): cross-origin
 credentials

Authorization, Cookie and Proxy-Authorization set through the http
stream context were sent again when follow_location went to another
scheme, host or port, leaking them to the redirect target. They are now
stripped there, and stay stripped for the rest of the redirect chain,
also when the header name is repeated or the bag uses odd line endings.

Backport of php-src 5af9465ca8 (Alexandre Daubois, Jakub Zelenka),
Sury's 7.4 patch 0152 with its test fix 0160 (Remi Collet). Sury
applies it on top of GH-11274 (0151, 307/308 keep POST), a behaviour
change and not a security fix, which we do not carry. So the strip
block keeps 7.4.33's "if (!header_init)" condition and the redirect
flags go straight into the recursive php_stream_url_wrap_http_ex()
call. HTTP_WRAPPER_STRIP_AUTH keeps upstream's value 8.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
