From 5ec70dcb89be676b2e5b5de61a74605ec59ea2d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:11:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-4w77-75f9-2c8w: use after free in the CLI server
 POST reader

The built-in web server (php -S) set request_info->content_type only
when the request had a Content-Type header, so a request without one
kept the pointer from the previous request, already freed, and
sapi_read_post_data() read it. We do not run php -S;
fixed for completeness.

Backport of php-src 7dd336ae83 (Niels Dossche), Sury's 7.4 patch 0098.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
