From 211f7ab250fdbc7305fa97c778db286f80cdee57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:11:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-h35g-vwh6-m678 (CVE-2024-8929): mysqlnd heap
 over-reads

A hostile or spoofed MySQL server could make mysqlnd read past its
packet buffers (COM_LIST field defaults, upsert filename, OK message,
binary row fields of every type) and return heap content to the script.
Also bounds the auth_protocol name in the greeting packet and stops
using an uninitialised struct in the result code.

Backport of php-src (Jakub Zelenka) as Sury's 7.4 patches 0100 (fix),
0101 (auth_protocol over-read), 0102 (uninitialised struct, Remi
Collet), 0103 and 0105 (tests on the fake server).

